Subject: [PATCH] Retain the One UI 9 platform label for the USB device bus

SM-G990E_THL adds a sysfs_ss_writable label for /bus/usb/devices. The
One UI 9 donor owns that exact path as sysfs_usb, so both labels cannot be
compiled together. Drop only the conflicting vendor genfscon; preserve
the donor policy and every unrelated device-specific label. No allow is
added to compensate for the old writable label.

diff --git a/vendor_sepolicy.cil b/vendor_sepolicy.cil
--- a/vendor_sepolicy.cil
+++ b/vendor_sepolicy.cil
@@ -758,7 +758,6 @@
 (genfscon sysfs /class/richtek_spm (u object_r sysfs_ss_writable ((s0) (s0))))
 (genfscon sysfs /power/over_limit (u object_r sysfs_power ((s0) (s0))))
 (genfscon sysfs /power/limit_stat (u object_r sysfs_ski_power_readable ((s0) (s0))))
-(genfscon sysfs /bus/usb/devices (u object_r sysfs_ss_writable ((s0) (s0))))
 (genfscon sysfs /devices/svc (u object_r sysfs_svc ((s0) (s0))))
 (genfscon sysfs /kernel/ehmp (u object_r sysfs_ehmp ((s0) (s0))))
 (genfscon sysfs /module/mcps (u object_r sysfs_ss_writable ((s0) (s0))))
